Changes:
1. Disabled AutoCommit in PostgreSQL (https://github.com/ClickHouse/clickhouse-jdbc-bridge/issues/161):
This change is required for stream processing.
2. Added boolean-to-string conversion for PostgreSQL:
This change prevents the error: Caused by: org.postgresql.util.PSQLException: Bad value for type int: t when querying boolean types.
For example:
SELECT * FROM jdbc('jdbc:postgresql://host:5432/microsoft_contoso_integration_100k?user=postgres&password=', 'SELECT true');
3. Fixed precision loss for numeric types (https://github.com/ClickHouse/clickhouse-jdbc-bridge/issues/160):
This resolves issues where precision was lost for numeric values.
For example:
SELECT * FROM jdbc('jdbc:postgresql://host:5432/microsoft_contoso_integration_100k?user=postgres&password=', 'SELECT 123.456789');
4. Enabled HTTP compression:
Compression has been enabled for future use.
5. Minor refactoring of the DataTableReader->process method:
This refactor slightly improves performance for wide tables.
6. Disabled useless and frequent exceptions in logs from io.vertx.core.impl.BlockedThreadChecker.
7. Increased DEFAULT_FETCH_SIZE from 1000 to 10,000:
This increase has shown to improve efficiency by 20-30% in our cases.
8. Updated dependencies and libraries for Java 21 LTS compatibility:
- Upgraded Java runtime from 1.8 to 21 LTS (Eclipse Temurin) with compatible Maven plugins and modernized JVM options (UseG1GC, UseStringDeduplication, ExitOnOutOfMemoryError)
- Updated Caffeine cache library from 2.9.3 to 3.2.1: Improved Java 21 LTS and GraalVM Native Image compatibility with performance optimizations and security updates
- Updated PostgreSQL JDBC Driver to 42.7.7: Latest stable release with enhanced security, Java 21 compatibility, and improved connection handling
- Updated HikariCP connection pool from 3.4.5 to 5.1.0: Java 21 LTS compatibility with enhanced performance monitoring and better resource management
- Updated dnsjava library from 3.5.0 to 3.6.3: Security fixes for CVE-2024-25638 and CVE-2023-50387 with improved DNS resolution and JPMS support
- Updated SLF4J logging framework from 1.7.36 to 2.0.17: Major version upgrade with improved performance, enhanced SPI, and Java 21 LTS compatibility
- Updated Vert.x framework from 3.9.13 to 4.5.1 with breaking changes adaptations: Major version upgrade with API adaptations, enhanced performance, and improved Java 21 LTS compatibility
9. Introduced Vert.x BOM (Bill of Materials) for centralized dependency management:
Added vertx-dependencies BOM to eliminate version conflicts and ensure compatibility across all Vert.x modules.
10. Updated Dockerfile to use Java 21 LTS base image:
Replaced adoptopenjdk/openjdk8-openj9 with eclipse-temurin:21.0.7_6-jre base image and updated JVM options for better performance and compatibility.
11. Updated JDBC drivers to latest secure versions to fix 7 HIGH vulnerabilities:
- clickhouse-jdbc: 0.3.2-patch8 → 0.9.0 (fixes CVE-2024-23689)
- mysql-connector-java: 8.0.28 → mysql-connector-j 9.1.0 (fixes CVE-2023-22102)
- neo4j-jdbc-driver: 4.0.5 → neo4j-jdbc-full-bundle 6.6.0 (fixes 4 Jackson CVEs)
- sqlite-jdbc: 3.36.0.3 → 3.45.3.0 (fixes CVE-2023-32697)